# RAG

## Mục tiêu

Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) là một pattern kết hợp retrieval systems với LLMs để generate responses dựa trên retrieved information. RAG giúp LLMs access current information, reduce hallucinations, và provide cited answers. Trong Cursor Enterprise Framework, RAG được sử dụng cho applications như AI assistants, knowledge bases, document Q&A, và customer support.

Mục tiêu của rule này là hướng dẫn developers trong việc implement RAG systems hiệu quả, từ document processing, embedding generation, vector storage, retrieval strategies, đến generation với context.

## Nguyên tắc

**1. Document Processing Pipeline**

Clean and normalize documents. Split into appropriate chunks. Preserve metadata. Handle various formats. Quality control.

**2. Chunking Strategy**

Choose chunk size carefully. 512-1024 tokens typical. Overlap for continuity. Consider semantic boundaries. Test different strategies.

**3. Embedding Quality**

Use appropriate embedding model. Match model to use case. Consider multilingual needs. Evaluate embedding quality. Update embeddings when needed.

**4. Vector Storage**

Choose appropriate vector database. Optimize for retrieval speed. Consider hybrid search. Index for performance. Monitor index health.

**5. Retrieval Strategy**

Use appropriate similarity metric. Combine with keyword search. Implement reranking. Consider user context. Optimize for recall/precision.

**6. Context Assembly**

Assemble retrieved context. Manage token budget. Prioritize relevant chunks. Add citations. Format for LLM.

**7. Generation with RAG**

Craft prompts with context. Instruct LLM to cite sources. Handle contradictions. Set appropriate temperature. Validate responses.

**8. Evaluation**

Measure retrieval quality. Evaluate generation quality. Use RAG metrics. A/B test strategies. Gather user feedback.

**9. Maintenance**

Update documents. Refresh embeddings. Monitor drift. Handle deletions. Maintain data quality.

**10. Scalability**

Design for document volume. Batch processing. Incremental updates. Distributed retrieval. Cost optimization.

## Checklist

- [ ] Document processing pipeline designed
- [ ] Chunking strategy selected
- [ ] Embedding model chosen
- [ ] Vector database configured
- [ ] Retrieval logic implemented
- [ ] Reranking strategy defined
- [ ] Prompt template designed
- [ ] Evaluation metrics set up
- [ ] Monitoring configured
- [ ] Update pipeline implemented

## Anti Pattern

**1. Poor Chunking**

Too large chunks. Too small chunks. Breaking semantic units. Ignoring document structure. No overlap.

**2. Single Retrieval**

No reranking. No hybrid search. No context weighting. Poor recall. Poor precision.

**3. Ignoring Token Limits**

No context budget. Exceeding LLM limits. Truncating randomly. Poor responses. Wasted tokens.

**4. Stale Knowledge**

No update pipeline. Outdated embeddings. Changed documents not reflected. Misleading answers.

**5. No Evaluation**

No retrieval metrics. No generation metrics. Blind optimization. Poor quality. User complaints.

## Best Practice

**1. Document Processing**

```typescript
// services/document-processor.service.ts
import { RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter } from 'langchain/text_splitter';
import { PDFLoader } from 'langchain/document_loaders/fs/pdf';
import { DocxLoader } from 'langchain/document_loaders/fs/docx';

interface ProcessedDocument {
  id: string;
  chunks: DocumentChunk[];
  metadata: DocumentMetadata;
}

interface DocumentChunk {
  id: string;
  content: string;
  embedding?: number[];
  metadata: ChunkMetadata;
}

interface DocumentMetadata {
  source: string;
  title?: string;
  author?: string;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
  type: 'pdf' | 'docx' | 'txt' | 'html';
}

interface ChunkMetadata {
  chunkIndex: number;
  totalChunks: number;
  charCount: number;
  tokenEstimate: number;
}

class DocumentProcessor {
  private textSplitter: RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter;
  private embeddingService: EmbeddingService;

  constructor(
    chunkSize: number = 1000,
    chunkOverlap: number = 200
  ) {
    this.textSplitter = new RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter({
      chunkSize,
      chunkOverlap,
      separators: ['\n\n', '\n', '. ', ' ', ''],
    });
    this.embeddingService = new EmbeddingService();
  }

  async processDocument(
    filePath: string,
    metadata: Partial<DocumentMetadata>
  ): Promise<ProcessedDocument> {
    const extension = filePath.split('.').pop()?.toLowerCase();
    let loader;

    switch (extension) {
      case 'pdf':
        loader = new PDFLoader(filePath);
        break;
      case 'docx':
        loader = new DocxLoader(filePath);
        break;
      default:
        loader = new TextLoader(filePath);
    }

    const docs = await loader.load();
    const fullText = docs.map(d => d.pageContent).join('\n\n');

    // Split into chunks
    const chunks = await this.textSplitter.splitText(fullText);
    
    // Generate embeddings
    const embeddings = await this.embeddingService.createBatchEmbeddings(chunks);

    // Create chunk objects
    const processedChunks: DocumentChunk[] = chunks.map((content, index) => {
      const tokenEstimate = Math.ceil(content.length / 4);
      
      return {
        id: `${metadata.source}-chunk-${index}`,
        content,
        embedding: embeddings[index],
        metadata: {
          chunkIndex: index,
          totalChunks: chunks.length,
          charCount: content.length,
          tokenEstimate,
        },
      };
    });

    return {
      id: metadata.source || crypto.randomUUID(),
      chunks: processedChunks,
      metadata: {
        source: metadata.source || 'unknown',
        title: metadata.title,
        author: metadata.author,
        createdAt: metadata.createdAt || new Date(),
        updatedAt: new Date(),
        type: (extension || 'txt') as any,
      },
    };
  }

  async processText(
    text: string,
    source: string,
    additionalMetadata: Record<string, any> = {}
  ): Promise<ProcessedDocument> {
    const chunks = await this.textSplitter.splitText(text);
    const embeddings = await this.embeddingService.createBatchEmbeddings(chunks);

    const processedChunks: DocumentChunk[] = chunks.map((content, index) => ({
      id: `${source}-chunk-${index}`,
      content,
      embedding: embeddings[index],
      metadata: {
        chunkIndex: index,
        totalChunks: chunks.length,
        charCount: content.length,
        tokenEstimate: Math.ceil(content.length / 4),
      },
    }));

    return {
      id: source,
      chunks: processedChunks,
      metadata: {
        source,
        ...additionalMetadata,
        createdAt: new Date(),
        updatedAt: new Date(),
        type: 'txt' as const,
      },
    };
  }
}
```

**2. Vector Storage**

```typescript
// services/vector-store.service.ts
import { Pinecone } from '@pinecone-database/pinecone';
import { supabase } from '@/lib/supabase';

interface VectorRecord {
  id: string;
  values: number[];
  metadata?: Record<string, any>;
}

interface RetrievalResult {
  id: string;
  score: number;
  content: string;
  metadata: Record<string, any>;
}

class VectorStore {
  private pinecone: Pinecone;
  private indexName: string;
  private useSupabase: boolean;

  constructor(useSupabase: boolean = false) {
    this.pinecone = new Pinecone({
      apiKey: process.env.PINECONE_API_KEY!,
    });
    this.useSupabase = useSupabase;
    this.indexName = process.env.PINECONE_INDEX || 'knowledge-base';
  }

  async upsertChunks(chunks: DocumentChunk[]): Promise<void> {
    if (this.useSupabase) {
      await this.upsertToSupabase(chunks);
    } else {
      await this.upsertToPinecone(chunks);
    }
  }

  private async upsertToPinecone(chunks: DocumentChunk[]): Promise<void> {
    const index = this.pinecone.Index(this.indexName);

    const vectors: VectorRecord[] = chunks.map(chunk => ({
      id: chunk.id,
      values: chunk.embedding || [],
      metadata: {
        content: chunk.content,
        ...chunk.metadata,
      },
    }));

    // Batch upsert
    const batchSize = 100;
    for (let i = 0; i < vectors.length; i += batchSize) {
      const batch = vectors.slice(i, i + batchSize);
      await index.upsert(batch);
    }
  }

  private async upsertToSupabase(chunks: DocumentChunk[]): Promise<void> {
    const records = chunks.map(chunk => ({
      id: chunk.id,
      content: chunk.content,
      embedding: chunk.embedding,
      metadata: chunk.metadata,
    }));

    const { error } = await supabase
      .from('document_chunks')
      .upsert(records, { onConflict: 'id' });

    if (error) throw error;
  }

  async retrieve(
    queryEmbedding: number[],
    options: {
      topK?: number;
      filter?: Record<string, any>;
      namespace?: string;
    } = {}
  ): Promise<RetrievalResult[]> {
    if (this.useSupabase) {
      return this.retrieveFromSupabase(queryEmbedding, options);
    } else {
      return this.retrieveFromPinecone(queryEmbedding, options);
    }
  }

  private async retrieveFromPinecone(
    queryEmbedding: number[],
    options: { topK?: number; filter?: Record<string, any>; namespace?: string }
  ): Promise<RetrievalResult[]> {
    const index = this.pinecone.Index(this.indexName);
    
    const queryResponse = await index.query({
      vector: queryEmbedding,
      topK: options.topK || 10,
      filter: options.filter,
      namespace: options.namespace,
      includeMetadata: true,
    });

    return (queryResponse.matches || []).map(match => ({
      id: match.id,
      score: match.score || 0,
      content: match.metadata?.content || '',
      metadata: match.metadata || {},
    }));
  }

  private async retrieveFromSupabase(
    queryEmbedding: number[],
    options: { topK?: number; filter?: Record<string, any> }
  ): Promise<RetrievalResult[]> {
    const { data, error } = await supabase.rpc('match_documents', {
      query_embedding: queryEmbedding,
      match_threshold: 0.7,
      match_count: options.topK || 10,
    });

    if (error) throw error;

    return (data || []).map(row => ({
      id: row.id,
      score: row.similarity,
      content: row.content,
      metadata: row.metadata || {},
    }));
  }

  async deleteBySource(source: string): Promise<void> {
    if (this.useSupabase) {
      await supabase
        .from('document_chunks')
        .delete()
        .eq('metadata->>source', source);
    } else {
      const index = this.pinecone.Index(this.indexName);
      // Note: Pinecone requires prefix-based deletion
      // This is a simplified example
      await index.deleteMany({ filter: { source } });
    }
  }
}
```

**3. Retrieval với Reranking**

```typescript
// services/retrieval.service.ts
interface RetrievalOptions {
  query: string;
  queryEmbedding: number[];
  filters?: Record<string, any>;
  maxResults?: number;
  rerank?: boolean;
  rerankTopK?: number;
}

interface RerankedResult extends RetrievalResult {
  rerankScore?: number;
  positions?: number[];
}

class RetrievalService {
  constructor(
    private vectorStore: VectorStore,
    private embeddingService: EmbeddingService,
    private reranker?: RerankerService
  ) {}

  async retrieve(options: RetrievalOptions): Promise<RerankedResult[]> {
    const {
      query,
      queryEmbedding,
      filters,
      maxResults = 20,
      rerank = true,
      rerankTopK = 10
    } = options;

    // Initial retrieval - get more results for reranking
    let results = await this.vectorStore.retrieve(queryEmbedding, {
      topK: rerank ? maxResults : maxResults,
      filter: filters,
    });

    if (rerank && this.reranker && rerankTopK < results.length) {
      // Rerank using cross-encoder
      const reranked = await this.reranker.rerank(
        query,
        results.map(r => r.content),
        { topK: rerankTopK }
      );

      // Merge scores
      results = reranked.map((r, index) => ({
        ...results[r.index],
        rerankScore: r.score,
        positions: [index],
      }));
    }

    // Deduplicate by source
    const seen = new Set<string>();
    const deduplicated: RerankedResult[] = [];

    for (const result of results) {
      const source = result.metadata.source;
      if (!seen.has(source)) {
        seen.add(source);
        deduplicated.push(result);
      }
    }

    return deduplicated.slice(0, maxResults);
  }

  async hybridRetrieve(
    query: string,
    filters?: Record<string, any>,
    maxResults: number = 10
  ): Promise<RetrievalResult[]> {
    // Generate query embedding
    const queryEmbedding = await this.embeddingService.createEmbedding(query);

    // Vector search
    const vectorResults = await this.retrieve({
      query,
      queryEmbedding,
      filters,
      maxResults: maxResults * 2,
      rerank: true,
      rerankTopK: maxResults,
    });

    // Keyword search (if using pgvector)
    const keywordResults = await this.keywordSearch(query, filters, maxResults);

    // Combine results using Reciprocal Rank Fusion
    const fused = this.reciprocalRankFusion(
      vectorResults.map((r, i) => ({ id: r.id, score: 1 / (i + 61) })),
      keywordResults.map((r, i) => ({ id: r.id, score: 1 / (i + 61) }))
    );

    // Map back to full results
    const resultMap = new Map([
      ...vectorResults.map(r => [r.id, r]),
      ...keywordResults.map(r => [r.id, r]),
    ]);

    return fused
      .map(f => resultMap.get(f.id))
      .filter((r): r is RetrievalResult => !!r);
  }

  private reciprocalRankFusion(
    ...rankings: Array<Array<{ id: string; score: number }>>
  ): Array<{ id: string; score: number }> {
    const scores = new Map<string, number>();

    for (const ranking of rankings) {
      for (let i = 0; i < ranking.length; i++) {
        const { id, score } = ranking[i];
        const current = scores.get(id) || 0;
        scores.set(id, current + score);
      }
    }

    return Array.from(scores.entries())
      .map(([id, score]) => ({ id, score }))
      .sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);
  }

  private async keywordSearch(
    query: string,
    filters?: Record<string, any>,
    limit: number = 10
  ): Promise<RetrievalResult[]> {
    // Implementation depends on your keyword search backend
    // Could be pgvector full-text search, Elasticsearch, etc.
    return [];
  }
}
```

**4. RAG Generation**

```typescript
// services/rag.service.ts
interface RAGOptions {
  query: string;
  maxContextTokens?: number;
  temperature?: number;
  model?: string;
  filters?: Record<string, any>;
}

interface RAGResponse {
  answer: string;
  sources: Array<{
    id: string;
    content: string;
    score: number;
    metadata: Record<string, any>;
  }>;
  tokensUsed: {
    prompt: number;
    completion: number;
  };
}

class RAGService {
  constructor(
    private retrievalService: RetrievalService,
    private llmService: ClaudeService | OpenAIService,
    private embeddingService: EmbeddingService,
    private maxContextTokens: number = 150000
  ) {}

  async query(options: RAGOptions): Promise<RAGResponse> {
    const {
      query,
      maxContextTokens = 120000,
      temperature = 0.3,
      model = 'claude-sonnet-4',
      filters
    } = options;

    // Generate query embedding
    const queryEmbedding = await this.embeddingService.createEmbedding(query);

    // Retrieve relevant chunks
    const retrieved = await this.retrievalService.retrieve({
      query,
      queryEmbedding,
      filters,
      maxResults: 20,
      rerank: true,
      rerankTopK: 10,
    });

    // Assemble context within token budget
    const context = this.assembleContext(retrieved, maxContextTokens - 2000); // Reserve for prompt

    // Generate answer
    const systemPrompt = `You are a helpful AI assistant. Use the provided context to answer the user's question. Follow these rules:

1. Only use information from the provided context
2. If the context doesn't contain enough information, say so
3. Always cite your sources using [Source N] notation
4. Be concise but thorough
5. If you're uncertain, acknowledge it`;

    const userPrompt = `Context:
${context}

Question: ${query}

Answer the question based on the context above.`;

    const response = await this.llmService.createMessage(
      [
        { role: 'user', content: userPrompt }
      ],
      systemPrompt,
      { model, temperature, maxTokens: 2048 }
    );

    return {
      answer: response.content[0].text || response.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || '',
      sources: retrieved.slice(0, 5).map((r, i) => ({
        id: r.id,
        content: r.content.slice(0, 500) + (r.content.length > 500 ? '...' : ''),
        score: r.score,
        metadata: r.metadata,
      })),
      tokensUsed: {
        prompt: response.usage?.input_tokens || 0,
        completion: response.usage?.output_tokens || 0,
      },
    };
  }

  private assembleContext(
    results: RetrievalResult[],
    maxTokens: number
  ): string {
    const chunks: string[] = [];
    let totalTokens = 0;

    for (const result of results) {
      const tokenEstimate = Math.ceil(result.content.length / 4);
      
      if (totalTokens + tokenEstimate > maxTokens) {
        break;
      }

      chunks.push(`[Source ${chunks.length + 1}]: ${result.content}`);
      totalTokens += tokenEstimate;
    }

    return chunks.join('\n\n');
  }

  async queryStream(
    options: RAGOptions,
    onChunk: (chunk: string) => void
  ): Promise<RAGResponse> {
    const {
      query,
      maxContextTokens = 120000,
      temperature = 0.3,
      model = 'claude-sonnet-4',
      filters
    } = options;

    const queryEmbedding = await this.embeddingService.createEmbedding(query);

    const retrieved = await this.retrievalService.retrieve({
      query,
      queryEmbedding,
      filters,
      maxResults: 10,
      rerank: true,
    });

    const context = this.assembleContext(retrieved, maxContextTokens - 2000);

    const systemPrompt = `You are a helpful AI assistant. Use the provided context to answer the user's question. Always cite your sources using [Source N] notation.`;

    const userPrompt = `Context:
${context}

Question: ${query}`;

    // Stream response
    let fullResponse = '';
    
    if ('streamMessage' in this.llmService) {
      for await (const chunk of this.llmService.streamMessage(
        [{ role: 'user', content: userPrompt }],
        systemPrompt,
        { model, temperature }
      )) {
        fullResponse += chunk;
        onChunk(chunk);
      }
    } else {
      const response = await this.llmService.createMessage(
        [{ role: 'user', content: userPrompt }],
        systemPrompt,
        { model, temperature }
      );
      fullResponse = response.choices?.[0]?.message?.content || '';
      onChunk(fullResponse);
    }

    return {
      answer: fullResponse,
      sources: retrieved.slice(0, 5).map((r, i) => ({
        id: r.id,
        content: r.content.slice(0, 500),
        score: r.score,
        metadata: r.metadata,
      })),
      tokensUsed: { prompt: 0, completion: 0 },
    };
  }
}
```

**5. Evaluation Metrics**

```typescript
// services/rag-evaluation.service.ts
interface RAGEvaluationResult {
  retrieval: {
    precision: number;
    recall: number;
    f1: number;
    mrr: number;
    ndcg: number;
  };
  generation: {
    faithfulness: number;
    answerRelevancy: number;
    contextPrecision: number;
  };
  overall: number;
}

class RAGEvaluation {
  async evaluate(
    query: string,
    retrieved: RetrievalResult[],
    generated: string,
    groundTruth?: {
      relevantDocs?: string[];
      idealAnswer?: string;
    }
  ): Promise<RAGEvaluationResult> {
    const retrievalMetrics = this.evaluateRetrieval(
      retrieved,
      groundTruth?.relevantDocs || []
    );

    const generationMetrics = await this.evaluateGeneration(
      query,
      retrieved,
      generated,
      groundTruth?.idealAnswer
    );

    return {
      retrieval: retrievalMetrics,
      generation: generationMetrics,
      overall: (retrievalMetrics.f1 + generationMetrics.answerRelevancy) / 2,
    };
  }

  private evaluateRetrieval(
    retrieved: RetrievalResult[],
    relevant: string[]
  ): { precision: number; recall: number; f1: number; mrr: number; ndcg: number } {
    if (relevant.length === 0) {
      return { precision: 0, recall: 0, f1: 0, mrr: 0, ndcg: 0 };
    }

    const relevantSet = new Set(relevant);
    const retrievedRelevant = retrieved.filter(r => relevantSet.has(r.id));
    const relevantRetrieved = retrievedRelevant.length;

    const precision = relevantRetrieved / retrieved.length;
    const recall = relevantRetrieved / relevant.length;
    const f1 = 2 * (precision * recall) / (precision + recall);

    // MRR (Mean Reciprocal Rank)
    let mrr = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < retrieved.length; i++) {
      if (relevantSet.has(retrieved[i].id)) {
        mrr = 1 / (i + 1);
        break;
      }
    }

    // NDCG (Normalized Discounted Cumulative Gain)
    let dcg = 0;
    let idcg = 0;
    for (let i = 0; i < retrieved.length; i++) {
      const relevance = relevantSet.has(retrieved[i].id) ? 1 : 0;
      dcg += relevance / Math.log2(i + 2);
    }
    for (let i = 0; i < relevant.length; i++) {
      idcg += 1 / Math.log2(i + 2);
    }
    const ndcg = idcg > 0 ? dcg / idcg : 0;

    return { precision, recall, f1, mrr, ndcg };
  }

  private async evaluateGeneration(
    query: string,
    retrieved: RetrievalResult[],
    generated: string,
    idealAnswer?: string
  ): Promise<{ faithfulness: number; answerRelevancy: number; contextPrecision: number }> {
    // Simplified evaluation - in production, use LLM-based evaluation
    
    // Faithfulness: Check if answer mentions are in context
    const contextContents = retrieved.map(r => r.content.toLowerCase());
    const answerWords = generated.toLowerCase().split(/\s+/);
    const mentionedInContext = answerWords.filter(word => 
      contextContents.some(c => c.includes(word))
    ).length;
    const faithfulness = mentionedInContext / answerWords.length;

    // Answer relevancy: Compare with query
    const answerRelevancy = this.cosineSimilarity(
      await this.getEmbedding(query),
      await this.getEmbedding(generated)
    );

    // Context precision
    const contextPrecision = retrieved.slice(0, 5).length / 5;

    return { faithfulness, answerRelevancy, contextPrecision };
  }

  private async getEmbedding(text: string): Promise<number[]> {
    // Use embedding service
    return [];
  }

  private cosineSimilarity(a: number[], b: number[]): number {
    const dot = a.reduce((sum, val, i) => sum + val * b[i], 0);
    const magA = Math.sqrt(a.reduce((sum, val) => sum + val * val, 0));
    const magB = Math.sqrt(b.reduce((sum, val) => sum + val * val, 0));
    return dot / (magA * magB);
  }
}
```

## Workflow

**Phase 1: Data Preparation**

Collect documents. Clean and format. Design metadata. Plan chunking strategy.

**Phase 2: Processing Pipeline**

Implement document loader. Create chunker. Generate embeddings. Store in vector DB.

**Phase 3: Retrieval Development**

Implement retrieval. Add reranking. Test retrieval quality. Optimize.

**Phase 4: Generation Integration**

Design prompt template. Integrate with LLM. Add streaming. Test responses.

**Phase 5: Evaluation**

Set up metrics. Evaluate retrieval. Evaluate generation. Iterate.

**Phase 6: Production**

Deploy pipeline. Set up monitoring. Configure updates. Maintain quality.

